Spherical harmonics
-------------------
cpp/include/arlamx/orbit/gravity.hpp and cpp/src/orbit/gravity.cpp evaluate
the standard spherical-harmonic geopotential (Montenbruck & Gill; Holmes &
Featherstone) on GRACE GGM03S coefficients. They are an independent
implementation. They do not include Basilisk source and the plant does not
link Basilisk.

The reference model for those segments is:

  SphericalHarmonicsGravityModel
  Basilisk
  Autonomous Vehicle Systems Laboratory
  University of Colorado Boulder
  https://github.com/AVSLab/basilisk
  License: ISC
  Copyright (c) Autonomous Vehicle Systems Lab,
  University of Colorado at Boulder

Cite Basilisk when you reuse those segments or when you publish a result
that depends on them. The comparison lives in tests/basilisk_ref/.

Third-party data, not covered by the MIT license
-------------------------------------------------
data/GGM03S.txt is a GRACE gravity model from the Center for Space Research
at The University of Texas at Austin / NASA. data/WMM.COF and data/WMM2025.COF
are World Magnetic Model coefficients from NOAA, the NGA, and the BGS.
Those files keep the terms of their authors.

